{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"ammoniacal-unempty-lowchen","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Advisory from S6 (6f14) LLM code review (Gerrit 1850). infra/Dockerfile.opcert runs the op-cert service as root (no USER directive). Container-hardening best practice is a dedicated non-root UID. RISK requiring care: the deployed signer reads a bind-mounted 0600 private key; a non-root container user needs a UID matching the mounted file's owner or the key becomes unreadable and startup fails. Remediation must coordinate the Dockerfile USER/UID with the compose bind-mount ownership in infra/compose. Deferred from S6 to avoid breaking the deploy on a rushed UID/mount-perms change.","id":"7237-b398-f72f-4634","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Add non-root USER to Dockerfile.opcert (coordinate with 0600 mounted key ownership)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787036471763614001,"uuid":"19e82a5b-6a30-4f36-8d39-2e48f1bb7dfb"}